  "notes": "{付|つ}く is an intransitive godan verb meaning something attaches or sticks by itself.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive): {付|つ}く - something attaches\n- {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive): {付|つ}ける - to attach something\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{付|つ}いている indicates a resulting state: \"is attached/stuck.\"\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {気|き}が{付|つ}く: to notice, become aware\n- {身|み}に{付|つ}く: to acquire (a skill), to learn\n- {運|うん}が{付|つ}く: to be lucky\n- {嘘|うそ}が{付|つ}く: to lie (different kanji: {嘘|うそ}をつく)\n- 〜{付|つ}き: with 〜 included ({朝食|ちょうしょく}{付|つ}き = with breakfast)",
